      Describes the types of trust boundaries implemented by Google Chrome and Firefox.
    </a:Description><a:Hidden>false</a:Hidden><a:Id>SE.TB.B.TMCore.NonIEB</a:Id><a:ImageLocation>Before label</a:ImageLocation><a:ImageSource>iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAQCAYAAAAf8/9hAAAABGdBTUEAALGPC/xhBQAAAAlwSFlzAAAOxAAADsQBlSsOGwAAABl0RVh0U29mdHdhcmUAQWRvYmUgSW1hZ2VSZWFkeXHJZTwAAABGSURBVDhPY/hPIWBQ9Ev6z2jqDccPnr0ESxArzoDMAeEDZy+DFRIrDjeAVDCcDIDyyQajgTioAhGEQekdHx+bGIUGeP8HAJ4fIfJijo6MAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC</a:ImageSource><a:ImageStream i:nil="true"/><a:Name>Other Browsers Boundaries</a:Name><a:ParentId>GE.TB.B</a:ParentId><a:Representation>BorderBoundary</a:Representation><a:Shape i:nil="true"/></a:ElementType></a:StandardElements><a:ThreatCategories><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>S</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Spoofing</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>T</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Tampering</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>R</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Repudiation</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>I</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Information Disclosure</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>D</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Denial Of Service</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>E</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory><a:ThreatCategory><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Id>A</a:Id><a:LongDescription/><a:Name>Abuse</a:Name><a:ShortDescription>Abuse is when a legitimate user violates the terms of use for the system without violating a system security policy.</a:ShortDescription></a:ThreatCategory></a:ThreatCategories><a:ThreatMetaData><IsPriorityUsed>true</IsPriorityUsed><IsStatusUsed>true</IsStatusUsed><PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Title</Name><Label>Title</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>ae1169ad-d70d-5c30-b1ff-e7f34ab676a5</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatCategory</Name><Label>Category</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values i:nil="true" xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"/><Id i:nil="true"/></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string><b:string>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</b:string><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string><b:string>Abuse is when a legitimate user violates the terms of use for the system without violating a system security policy.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>StateInformation</Name><Label>Justification</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>6c35d7f8-4667-5e8e-8819-d071a6418afa</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>InteractionString</Name><Label>Interaction</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values i:nil="true" xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"/><Id>1a1fad58-ca84-57e1-8358-0a7556d9121d</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string><b:string>Medium</b:string><b:string>Low</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SR - Security requirements</b:string><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string><b:string>SI - Secure implementation</b:string><b:string>SVV - Security verification and validation</b:string><b:string>DM - Security defect management</b:string><b:string>SUM - Security update management</b:string><b:string>SG - Security guidelines</b:string><b:string>SM - Security management and supply chain</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string><b:string>FR6 Timely response to events</b:string><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string><b:string>SL 2</b:string><b:string>SL 3</b:string><b:string>SL 4</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Likelihood</Name><Label>Likelihood (1-5)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>1 - Rare or negligible</b:string><b:string>2 - Unlikely or minor</b:string><b:string>3 - Possible or moderate</b:string><b:string>4 - Likely or major</b:string><b:string>5 - Almost certain or severe</b:string></Values><Id>Likelihood</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ImpactScore</Name><Label>Impact (1-5)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>1 - Rare or negligible</b:string><b:string>2 - Unlikely or minor</b:string><b:string>3 - Possible or moderate</b:string><b:string>4 - Likely or major</b:string><b:string>5 - Almost certain or severe</b:string></Values><Id>ImpactScore</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>RiskRating</Name><Label>Risk Rating</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not assessed</b:string><b:string>Critical 20-25</b:string><b:string>High 12-19</b:string><b:string>Medium 6-11</b:string><b:string>Low 1-5</b:string></Values><Id>RiskRating</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Treatment</Name><Label>Risk Treatment</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Not decided</b:string><b:string>Mitigate</b:string><b:string>Accept</b:string><b:string>Transfer to asset owner or integrator</b:string><b:string>Avoid</b:string></Values><Id>Treatment</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ImplementedMitigations</Name><Label>Implemented Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>ImplementedMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Validation</Name><Label>Verification Evidence (4-1 SVV)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>Validation</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Ownership</Name><Label>Owner</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string/></Values><Id>Ownership</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></PropertiesMetaData></a:ThreatMetaData><a:ThreatTypes><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker on the network path could impersonate {source.Name} and send traffic that {target.Name} accepts as genuine, because the communication crosses a trust boundary and the peer identity may not be verified.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-S01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker on the network path could impersonate {source.Name} and send traffic that {target.Name} accepts as genuine, because the communication crosses a trust boundary and the peer identity may not be verified.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Authenticate software processes and devices at the boundary (certificates or keys per device, not shared secrets). Reject traffic from unauthenticated peers. Allow-list expected peers on the conduit device.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0849 Masquerading; T0848 Rogue Master</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 1.2; 3-3 SR 1.2; 4-2 CR 1.8; 4-2 CR 1.9</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Manipulation of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofing of {source.Name} across a zone / trust boundary</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Traffic between {source.Name} and {target.Name} crosses a trust boundary without integrity protection, so an attacker in the path could modify values, commands or responses without detection.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(((flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Integrity only' or flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Integrity and encryption') or flow.providesIntegrity is 'Yes') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Traffic between {source.Name} and {target.Name} crosses a trust boundary without integrity protection, so an attacker in the path could modify values, commands or responses without detection.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use protocol security with message integrity (OPC UA Sign/SignAndEncrypt, CIP Security, DNP3-SA, IEC 62351, TLS). Where the protocol cannot be secured, tunnel it through an authenticated, integrity-protected conduit (IPsec/TLS) and restrict paths at the zone boundary.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0830 Adversary-in-the-Middle; T0831 Manipulation of Control; T0832 Manipulation of View</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.1; 3-3 SR 3.1; 4-2 CR 4.3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of control; Manipulation of view; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Adversary-in-the-middle tampering of {source.Name} to {target.Name} traffic</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Traffic between {source.Name} and {target.Name} is not encrypted across the trust boundary. An attacker could capture process values, tag names, program contents or credentials and use them to plan an attack.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(((flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Integrity and encryption') or flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Traffic between {source.Name} and {target.Name} is not encrypted across the trust boundary. An attacker could capture process values, tag names, program contents or credentials and use them to plan an attack.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Encrypt flows that cross zone boundaries where confidentiality is required (TLS, OPC UA SignAndEncrypt, IPsec tunnels). Classify data to decide where encryption is needed. Do not send credentials over unencrypted channels.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0842 Network Sniffing; T0861 Point &amp; Tag Identification; T0882 Theft of Operational Information</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.1; 4-2 CR 4.3; 3-3 SR 4.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Confidentiality / IP; Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Sniffing of operational data between {source.Name} and {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>The flow may carry passwords, keys or sensitive IP without encryption. Captured credentials allow an attacker to log in as a legitimate user or device.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>(flow.providesConfidentiality is 'Yes' or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow.CarriesSecrets is 'Unknown' or flow.CarriesSecrets is 'Yes') and (flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Unknown' or flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'None' or flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Integrity only')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The flow may carry passwords, keys or sensitive IP without encryption. Captured credentials allow an attacker to log in as a legitimate user or device.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Never transmit authenticators in cleartext. Use encrypted, mutually authenticated channels. Prefer challenge-response or certificate-based authentication. Rotate any credential that has been sent in cleartext.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0842 Network Sniffing; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.1; 4-2 CR 1.5; 4-2 CR 4.3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized access</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Credentials or keys exposed on the {source.Name} to {target.Name} flow</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Commands, setpoints or logic sent to {target.Name} are not authenticated, so recorded or crafted messages could be replayed or injected to operate equipment.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow.CarriesControl is 'Unknown' or flow.CarriesControl is 'Yes') and (flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'Unknown' or flow.ProtocolSecurity is 'None') and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Commands, setpoints or logic sent to {target.Name} are not authenticated, so recorded or crafted messages could be replayed or injected to operate equipment.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Protect session integrity with authenticated sessions, sequence numbers / nonces and timestamps (CR 3.8). Use protocol security with anti-replay (DNP3-SA, CIP Security, OPC UA). Validate that commands come from authorised masters only.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1692.001 Unauthorized Message: Command Message; T0831 Manipulation of Control</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.1; 4-2 CR 3.8; 4-2 CR 2.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Equipment damage; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Replay or injection of control commands to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} receives traffic from across a trust boundary. A flood, malformed-packet storm or resource-exhaustion attack could degrade or stop its essential functions.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} receives traffic from across a trust boundary. A flood, malformed-packet storm or resource-exhaustion attack could degrade or stop its essential functions.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Rate-limit and filter at the conduit. Design the component to keep essential functions running under load (CR 7.1) and test with network robustness tests (e.g. ISASecure CRT, Achilles-type storm tests). Separate control and management traffic.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SVV - Security verification and validation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0814 Denial of Service; T0826 Loss of Availability</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.1; 4-2 CR 7.2; 3-3 SR 7.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of availability; Loss of control; Loss of view</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Network flooding of {target.Name} from another zone</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>Requests that reach {target.Name} from another zone may not produce audit records, so changes, logins or failures could not be attributed or investigated.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-R01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Requests that reach {target.Name} from another zone may not produce audit records, so changes, logins or failures could not be attributed or investigated.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Generate audit records for access control, configuration changes, request errors and control-system events (CR 2.8) with accurate timestamps (CR 2.11). Make logs available to a central collector (CR 6.1).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SR - Security requirements</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0872 Indicator Removal on Host</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.8; 4-2 CR 2.11; 4-2 CR 6.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Forensics; Compliance</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Security-relevant actions on {target.Name} not audited</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Ports, services or debug functions on {target.Name} that are not needed for its function may be reachable from another zone and give an attacker extra attack surface.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E01</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Ports, services or debug functions on {target.Name} that are not needed for its function may be reachable from another zone and give an attacker extra attack surface.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Apply least functionality (CR 7.7): disable unused ports, services and protocols by default. Document required ports in the security guidelines. Allow only required flows at the conduit.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services; T0846 Remote System Discovery</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.7; 4-2 CR 7.6; 4-2 NDR 5.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Non-essential services on {target.Name} reachable across the boundary</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker could query {target.Name} across the boundary to identify vendor, model, firmware version, I/O modules and tags and so pick known vulnerabilities.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker could query {target.Name} across the boundary to identify vendor, model, firmware version, I/O modules and tags and so pick known vulnerabilities.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Low</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Limit information returned to unauthenticated requests. Require authentication for diagnostic and identification services where feasible. Detect scanning at the boundary.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0888 Remote System Information Discovery; T0846 Remote System Discovery</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.7; 4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 6.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Reconnaissance of {target.Name} (device fingerprinting, enumeration)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker with network access could download modified control logic or tasking to {target.Name}, changing how it controls the process (e.g. Stuxnet, TRITON).</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') and (flow.CarriesControl is 'Unknown' or flow.CarriesControl is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker with network access could download modified control logic or tasking to {target.Name}, changing how it controls the process (e.g. Stuxnet, TRITON).</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Require authentication and authorisation for program download, online edits and forcing (CR 2.1). Support a physical or logical write-protect / run-lock. Sign or integrity-check project files (CR 3.4). Log and alarm on every logic change.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0843 Program Download; T0821 Modify Controller Tasking; T0889 Modify Program; T0827 Loss of Control; T0879 Damage to Property</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 3.4; 4-2 CR 2.8</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Safety; Equipment damage</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Unauthorized program / logic download to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>A remote command could switch {target.Name} between Run, Program, Remote or Test modes without authorisation, enabling logic changes or stopping control.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>A remote command could switch {target.Name} between Run, Program, Remote or Test modes without authorisation, enabling logic changes or stopping control.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Require authorisation for mode changes. Provide a physical key switch or local confirmation for Program mode. Report the current mode to the HMI and alarm on unexpected changes.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0858 Change Operating Mode; T0868 Detect Operating Mode</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 2.8</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Loss of availability</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Unauthorized change of operating mode on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Protocol commands (stop CPU, reset, reboot) could be sent to {target.Name} to halt control of the process.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Protocol commands (stop CPU, reset, reboot) could be sent to {target.Name} to halt control of the process.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Require authorisation for stop/reset services. Make these services configurable and disabled by default where possible. Ensure outputs go to a defined safe state on stop (CR 3.6).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0816 Device Restart/Shutdown; T0813 Denial of Control; T0881 Service Stop</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.1; 4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 3.6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of production; Loss of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Remote restart, shutdown or stop of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker could upload the program and configuration from {target.Name} to steal know-how or study the process before an attack.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker could upload the program and configuration from {target.Name} to steal know-how or study the process before an attack.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Require authorisation for program upload. Support know-how protection (encrypted / protected blocks). Log upload events.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0845 Program Upload; T0882 Theft of Operational Information</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.1; 4-2 CR 2.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Confidentiality / IP; Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Program upload / theft of control logic from {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Parameters, setpoints or limits on {target.Name} could be changed to values outside the safe operating envelope.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') and (flow.CarriesControl is 'Unknown' or flow.CarriesControl is 'Yes')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Parameters, setpoints or limits on {target.Name} could be changed to values outside the safe operating envelope.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Validate all inputs against engineering limits (CR 3.5). Separate permissions for operator setpoints and engineering parameters. Keep hard limits in logic or in an independent safety layer, not only in the HMI.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SI - Secure implementation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0836 Modify Parameter; T0831 Manipulation of Control; T0827 Loss of Control; T0879 Damage to Property</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.5; 4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 3.6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Equipment damage; Product quality</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Setpoint or parameter on {target.Name} changed to unsafe values</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker could force inputs or outputs, or overwrite the I/O image, so {target.Name} acts on false values or drives outputs directly.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker could force inputs or outputs, or overwrite the I/O image, so {target.Name} acts on false values or drives outputs directly.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Restrict force and I/O override functions to authorised engineering roles. Show active forces on the HMI. Log and alarm on force events.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0835 Manipulate I/O Image; T0806 Brute Force I/O</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 2.8</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of control; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Manipulation of I/O image or forcing of points on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Firmware for {target.Name} could be replaced with a modified image that hides malicious behaviour or bricks the device.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.FieldUpdatable is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Firmware for {target.Name} could be replaced with a modified image that hides malicious behaviour or bricks the device.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Accept only firmware signed by the product supplier and verify the signature on the device before install (CR 3.4, EDR 3.10). Prevent rollback to vulnerable versions. Require authorisation to start firmware update mode.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1693.002 Modify Firmware: Module Firmware; T1693.001 Modify Firmware: System Firmware; T0800 Activate Firmware Update Mode</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.4; 4-2 EDR 3.10; 4-2 EDR 3.14</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Persistent compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Malicious or modified firmware loaded on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Without a verified boot chain, an attacker who can write to flash could run persistent unsigned code on {target.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Without a verified boot chain, an attacker who can write to flash could run persistent unsigned code on {target.Name}.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Implement secure / measured boot from a hardware root of trust (EDR 3.14). Provision supplier and asset-owner roots of trust securely (EDR 3.12, 3.13). Verify security functions at start-up (CR 3.3).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1693.001 Modify Firmware: System Firmware; T0851 Rootkit</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 EDR 3.14; 4-2 EDR 3.12; 4-2 EDR 3.13; 4-2 CR 3.3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Persistent compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Boot process or runtime integrity of {target.Name} bypassed</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>If {target.Name} is overloaded, crashes or loses communication, its outputs may hold an unsafe state or behave unpredictably.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>If {target.Name} is overloaded, crashes or loses communication, its outputs may hold an unsafe state or behave unpredictably.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Define deterministic fail-safe output behaviour (CR 3.6) and safe error handling (CR 3.7). Use communication watchdogs. Test behaviour under network storms and malformed traffic.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SVV - Security verification and validation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0813 Denial of Control; T0826 Loss of Availability; T0827 Loss of Control; T0879 Damage to Property</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.6; 4-2 CR 3.7; 4-2 CR 7.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Equipment damage</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{target.Name} outputs not driven to a safe state when attacked or failing</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Communication processing on {target.Name} may share CPU with the control task, so heavy or malformed traffic could increase scan time and miss control deadlines.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Communication processing on {target.Name} may share CPU with the control task, so heavy or malformed traffic could increase scan time and miss control deadlines.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Prioritise the control task over communication (CR 7.2 resource management). Limit connections and request rates. Test with load and robustness testing at all supported SLs.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SVV - Security verification and validation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0814 Denial of Service</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.1; 4-2 CR 7.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Product quality</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Network load disturbs the scan cycle of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Someone with physical access to {target.Name} could open the enclosure, replace modules, insert hardware implants or connect to internal buses.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.PhysicallyExposed is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T08</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Someone with physical access to {target.Name} could open the enclosure, replace modules, insert hardware implants or connect to internal buses.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Provide tamper resistance and tamper detection with alarming (EDR 3.11, required from SL 2). Use sealed enclosures and locked cabinets. Report tamper events to the monitoring system.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1693.002 Modify Firmware: Module Firmware (via physical access)</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 EDR 3.11; 4-2 CR 2.8</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Persistent compromise; Loss of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Physical tampering with {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>JTAG, UART consoles, USB service ports or test modes on {target.Name} could give root access, bypass authentication or dump firmware.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.DebugPorts is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>JTAG, UART consoles, USB service ports or test modes on {target.Name} could give root access, bypass authentication or dump firmware.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Disable or lock debug interfaces in production (EDR/HDR/NDR 2.13). Protect service ports with authentication. Document any remaining interfaces in the security guidelines.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1693.002 Modify Firmware: Module Firmware; T1693.001 Modify Firmware: System Firmware</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 EDR 2.13; 4-2 HDR 2.13; 4-2 NDR 2.13</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Debug or service interface on {target.Name} gives privileged access</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Keys, certificates or passwords stored on {target.Name} could be read from flash or memory, letting an attacker impersonate the device or decrypt traffic from many devices.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.StoresSecrets is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Keys, certificates or passwords stored on {target.Name} could be read from flash or memory, letting an attacker impersonate the device or decrypt traffic from many devices.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Store private keys in a secure element / TPM or protected memory. Use unique keys per device, never fleet-wide secrets. Erase secrets on decommissioning (CR 4.2).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1694.002 Insecure Credentials: Hardcoded Credentials; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.1; 4-2 CR 1.5; 4-2 CR 4.2; 4-2 EDR 3.11</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Fleet-wide compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Extraction of keys or credentials from {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>A device connected to the fieldbus or serial link could act as a rogue master or slave, sending commands to or impersonating devices that {target.Name} trusts.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') and ((flow.Medium is 'Serial or fieldbus') or (source is 'SE.EI.OT.FieldDevice3P' or source is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-S02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>A device connected to the fieldbus or serial link could act as a rogue master or slave, sending commands to or impersonating devices that {target.Name} trusts.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Restrict physical access to fieldbus segments. Use protocols with device authentication where available. Monitor for unexpected masters or addresses. Allow-list device addresses.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0848 Rogue Master; T1692.002 Unauthorized Message: Reporting Message</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 1.2; 3-3 SR 1.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Rogue master or rogue device on the fieldbus to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Values reported from {source.Name} to {target.Name} could be falsified, so the control system acts on wrong process data or operators see false conditions.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or source is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or source is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.FieldDevice3P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T09</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Values reported from {source.Name} to {target.Name} could be falsified, so the control system acts on wrong process data or operators see false conditions.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Authenticate devices and protect message integrity. Apply plausibility and cross-checks on critical measurements (redundant sensors, rate-of-change limits). Keep independent safety measurements for safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1692.002 Unauthorized Message: Reporting Message; T0832 Manipulation of View</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.1; 4-2 CR 3.5; 4-2 CR 1.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of view; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Spoofed measurement or status reported from {source.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker could change safety logic, trip points or configuration on {target.Name}, so a hazardous event is not prevented (e.g. TRITON/TRISIS).</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SafetyRelated is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T10</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker could change safety logic, trip points or configuration on {target.Name}, so a hazardous event is not prevented (e.g. TRITON/TRISIS).</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Require authorisation plus a physical key / local confirmation for safety program changes. Verify logic signatures. Keep the SIS engineering workstation in the safety zone and offline when not in use. Perform the SIS security risk assessment required by IEC 61511-1 clause 8.2.4.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0880 Loss of Safety; T0837 Loss of Protection; T0889 Modify Program; T0827 Loss of Control; T0879 Damage to Property</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.4; 4-2 CR 2.1; IEC 61511-1 8.2.4</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 3</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Environmental; Equipment damage</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Unauthorized modification of safety logic or configuration on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Remote bypass, maintenance override or mode-change commands could disable the safety function of {target.Name} while the process is running.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SafetyRelated is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Remote bypass, maintenance override or mode-change commands could disable the safety function of {target.Name} while the process is running.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Allow bypass and override only locally or with dual authorisation. Alarm and time-limit all bypasses. Show bypass status on the HMI and log it.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0858 Change Operating Mode; T0837 Loss of Protection; T0878 Alarm Suppression; T0827 Loss of Control; T0879 Damage to Property</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 2.8; IEC 61511</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 3</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Bypass, override or inhibit of safety function on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} accepts traffic from outside its zone. A compromise of the BPCS or another zone could then affect the safety function (loss of independence).</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.SafetyRelated is 'Yes'))) and (flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} accepts traffic from outside its zone. A compromise of the BPCS or another zone could then affect the safety function (loss of independence).</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Place safety functions in a separate zone. Allow only read-only or tightly controlled write flows from the BPCS. Use a dedicated conduit device with protocol filtering. Keep safety and non-safety functions independent (IEC 61511 layers of protection).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0880 Loss of Safety; T0886 Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.1; 3-3 SR 5.2; 4-2 CR 5.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 3</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Compromise of the control network reaches safety function {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Safety protocols (PROFIsafe, CIP Safety, FSoE) detect random errors on a black channel but are not designed against an intelligent attacker who can forge valid safety frames.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((flow.CarriesSafety is 'Yes') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO') or (source is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T11</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety protocols (PROFIsafe, CIP Safety, FSoE) detect random errors on a black channel but are not designed against an intelligent attacker who can forge valid safety frames.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Treat the safety channel as needing security: isolate it in the safety zone, block access from other zones, and add cryptographic protection where the protocol supports it. Include deliberate attacks in the safety/security co-engineering analysis.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0830 Adversary-in-the-Middle; T0880 Loss of Safety</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.1; 3-3 SR 5.1; IEC 61784-3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 3</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Deliberate manipulation of safety communication to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Process values, alarms or status shown by {target.Name} could be falsified, so operators do not see or misjudge the real process state.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T12</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Process values, alarms or status shown by {target.Name} could be falsified, so operators do not see or misjudge the real process state.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Protect integrity of data from controllers (CR 3.1). Protect HMI graphics and tag databases against modification (CR 3.4). Provide independent indications for critical variables.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0832 Manipulation of View; T1692.002 Unauthorized Message: Reporting Message</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.1; 4-2 CR 3.4</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of view; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Manipulation of view on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} could be made unavailable or frozen so operators lose visibility of the process.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} could be made unavailable or frozen so operators lose visibility of the process.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Provide redundancy for essential HMI/SCADA functions. Support fast recovery from known-good images (CR 7.4). Make frozen displays detectable (heartbeat / live indicator).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0815 Denial of View; T0829 Loss of View</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.1; 4-2 CR 7.3; 4-2 CR 7.4</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of view; Loss of production</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Loss of view on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Alarm limits, priorities or notifications on {target.Name} could be changed or suppressed to hide an attack or abnormal process condition.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T13</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Alarm limits, priorities or notifications on {target.Name} could be changed or suppressed to hide an attack or abnormal process condition.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Restrict alarm configuration to authorised roles. Log and report alarm configuration changes. Monitor for unexpected alarm shelving / suppression.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0878 Alarm Suppression; T0838 Modify Alarm Settings</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 2.8</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Loss of view</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Alarm suppression or modification on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Users of {target.Name} could perform actions beyond their role (e.g. operators changing engineering parameters) if authorisation is not enforced per role.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt') and (target is 'GE.P' and (target.UserAccounts is 'Unknown' or target.UserAccounts is 'Yes'))) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Users of {target.Name} could perform actions beyond their role (e.g. operators changing engineering parameters) if authorisation is not enforced per role.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Enforce role-based authorisation for all human users (CR 2.1), with least privilege and separation between operator, engineer and administrator roles. Support supervisor override for essential operations.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0859 Valid Accounts; T0890 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 1.3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Missing or weak role-based access control on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>R</a:Category><a:Description>If {source.Name} uses shared or generic accounts on {target.Name}, actions cannot be traced to an individual.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Engineer' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Admin' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') and (target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt' or target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-R02</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>If {source.Name} uses shared or generic accounts on {target.Name}, actions cannot be traced to an individual.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Uniquely identify and authenticate all human users (CR 1.1). Record user identity in audit records (CR 2.8). Use non-repudiation for critical actions where required at SL 3+ (CR 2.12).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SR - Security requirements</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.8; 4-2 CR 1.1; 4-2 CR 2.12</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Forensics; Compliance</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Actions by {source.Name} on {target.Name} cannot be attributed</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} could be infected with malware via network, removable media, phishing or vendor tools.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T14</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} could be infected with malware via network, removable media, phishing or vendor tools.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Support malware protection appropriate to the platform: application allow-listing, OS hardening or validated anti-malware (HDR/SAR 3.2). Only run signed code. Document compatible security software in the guidelines.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0863 User Execution; T1701 Command and Scripting Interpreter; T0865 Spearphishing Attachment</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 HDR 3.2; 4-2 SAR 3.2; 4-2 CR 3.4</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Malware execution on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Ransomware or wiper malware could encrypt or destroy {target.Name} and its data, stopping production (e.g. NotPetya, Colonial Pipeline effects).</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Ransomware or wiper malware could encrypt or destroy {target.Name} and its data, stopping production (e.g. NotPetya, Colonial Pipeline effects).</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Support backup of configuration and data (CR 7.3) and documented, tested recovery to a known secure state (CR 7.4). Limit lateral movement through segmentation and least privilege. Keep offline backups.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0809 Data Destruction; T0828 Loss of Productivity and Revenue; T0826 Loss of Availability</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.3; 4-2 CR 7.4; 3-3 SR 5.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of production; Financial</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Ransomware or destructive malware disables {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} may run on an OS or runtime that is out of support or rarely patched, exposing known vulnerabilities.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.LegacyOS is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} may run on an OS or runtime that is out of support or rarely patched, exposing known vulnerabilities.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Support the product on maintained platforms. Provide a patch qualification and delivery process (4-1 SUM) and timely security updates (HDR 3.10). Define compensating countermeasures for legacy deployments in the security guidelines.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SUM - Security update management</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services; T0890 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 HDR 3.10; 4-1 SUM; 4-1 SG</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Exploitation of unpatched / legacy platform of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Engineering projects handled by {target.Name} could be infected or modified so malicious logic is downloaded to controllers.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost') or (target is 'SE.DS.OT.ProjectFiles'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T15</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Engineering projects handled by {target.Name} could be infected or modified so malicious logic is downloaded to controllers.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Integrity-protect project files (signatures / hashes, CR 3.4). Show differences before download. Validate project files on open. Keep engineering tools patched and isolated.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0873 Project File Infection; T0889 Modify Program</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.4; 4-2 SAR 3.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Project file infection via {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Projects, network diagrams, tag lists or historical data on {target.Name} could be exfiltrated and used to plan an attack or steal IP.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.ProjectFiles' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.HistorianDB')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Projects, network diagrams, tag lists or historical data on {target.Name} could be exfiltrated and used to plan an attack or steal IP.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Encrypt sensitive data at rest (CR 4.1). Restrict read access by role. Monitor large exports. Classify engineering data.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0882 Theft of Operational Information; T0811 Data from Information Repositories; T0893 Data from Local System</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.1; 4-2 CR 2.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Confidentiality / IP; Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Theft of engineering / operational information from {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{source.Name} holds the privileges to program and configure {target.Name}. If it is compromised, an attacker inherits full control over the controller.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(source is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or source is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost') and (target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E08</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{source.Name} holds the privileges to program and configure {target.Name}. If it is compromised, an attacker inherits full control over the controller.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Make {target.Name} authenticate the engineering tool and user, not only the network address (CR 1.2, CR 1.1). Require re-authentication for critical operations. Harden and isolate engineering workstations; connect them only when needed.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0843 Program Download; T0886 Remote Services; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 1.1; 4-2 CR 1.2; 4-2 CR 2.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Safety</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Compromised {source.Name} used to control {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>The web interface of {target.Name} could be vulnerable to injection, XSS, CSRF, path traversal or authentication bypass, leading to device takeover.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.WebInterface is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E09</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The web interface of {target.Name} could be vulnerable to injection, XSS, CSRF, path traversal or authentication bypass, leading to device takeover.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Apply secure coding (OWASP ASVS) and input validation (CR 3.5). Use CSRF tokens, secure headers and HTTPS only. Perform web penetration testing and static analysis (4-1 SVV).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SI - Secure implementation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0819 Exploit Public-Facing Application; T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.5; 4-2 CR 2.1; 4-1 SI; 4-1 SVV</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Web application vulnerabilities in {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>Session tokens for {target.Name} could be stolen or fixed, allowing an attacker to act as a logged-in user.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.WebInterface is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-S03</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Session tokens for {target.Name} could be stolen or fixed, allowing an attacker to act as a logged-in user.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Protect session integrity (CR 3.8): random session IDs, secure/HttpOnly cookies, invalidate on logout. Session lock after inactivity (CR 2.5) and remote session termination (CR 2.6).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SI - Secure implementation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.8; 4-2 CR 2.5; 4-2 CR 2.6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized access</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Session hijacking on the {target.Name} web interface</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Scripts, macros or mobile code (JavaScript, VBA, HMI scripts) executed by {target.Name} could be injected or modified.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T16</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Scripts, macros or mobile code (JavaScript, VBA, HMI scripts) executed by {target.Name} could be injected or modified.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Control mobile code (SAR 2.4): allow only authorised, integrity-checked scripts. Disable scripting features that are not needed.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1701 Command and Scripting Interpreter; T0871 Execution through API</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 SAR 2.4; 4-2 CR 3.4</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Mobile code or script injection in {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>A user at {target.Name} could escape the HMI shell (dialogs, help files, keyboard shortcuts) to the desktop and gain OS-level access.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC') and (source is 'SE.EI.OT.Operator' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Engineer' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Admin' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E10</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>A user at {target.Name} could escape the HMI shell (dialogs, help files, keyboard shortcuts) to the desktop and gain OS-level access.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Harden kiosk mode: block shortcuts, file dialogs and shell access. Run HMI under a least-privilege account. Apply least functionality to the host (CR 7.7).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SG - Security guidelines</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0823 Graphical User Interface</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.1; 4-2 CR 7.7</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Kiosk / HMI break-out to the underlying OS of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Error messages, stack traces or diagnostic pages from {target.Name} could reveal versions, paths or configuration useful to an attacker.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((((target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.WebInterface is 'Yes'))) or (target is 'SE.P.OT.HMI' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SCADA' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EngTool' or target is 'SE.P.OT.HistorianApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.OPCServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WebServer' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EdgeApp' or target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AuthService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SecurityMonitor' or target is 'SE.P.OT.BackupService' or target is 'SE.P.OT.AssetMgmt'))) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Error messages, stack traces or diagnostic pages from {target.Name} could reveal versions, paths or configuration useful to an attacker.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Low</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Return error information that supports operation without exposing internals (CR 3.7). Restrict diagnostic data to authenticated users.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SI - Secure implementation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0888 Remote System Information Discovery</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.7</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Verbose errors or diagnostics disclose internals of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} could ship with default, shared or hard-coded passwords or keys that attackers can find in manuals or firmware.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.UserAccounts is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'GE.P')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-S04</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} could ship with default, shared or hard-coded passwords or keys that attackers can find in manuals or firmware.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>No hard-coded credentials. Force change of default credentials at commissioning (CR 1.5). Enforce password strength (CR 1.7). Support unique per-device credentials.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1694.001 Insecure Credentials: Default Credentials; T1694.002 Insecure Credentials: Hardcoded Credentials</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 1.1; 4-2 CR 1.5; 4-2 CR 1.7</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized access</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Default, shared or hard-coded credentials on {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker could repeatedly try passwords on {target.Name} if failed attempts are not limited.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.UserAccounts is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'GE.P')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-S05</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker could repeatedly try passwords on {target.Name} if failed attempts are not limited.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Limit unsuccessful login attempts (CR 1.11) without blocking essential functions. Obscure authenticator feedback (CR 1.10). Log failed logins. Support MFA for remote / untrusted network access (CR 1.1 RE).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 1.11; 4-2 CR 1.10; 4-2 CR 1.7</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Unauthorized access</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Brute-force or password guessing against {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Malformed protocol messages could trigger buffer overflows or parser errors in {target.Name}, causing crashes or remote code execution.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'GE.P')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E11</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Malformed protocol messages could trigger buffer overflows or parser errors in {target.Name}, causing crashes or remote code execution.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Validate all input (CR 3.5). Use memory-safe languages or compiler hardening. Fuzz-test every protocol interface (4-1 SVV-3) and run communication robustness tests.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SVV - Security verification and validation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services; T0890 Exploitation for Privilege Escalation; T0820 Exploitation for Evasion</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.5; 4-1 SI; 4-1 SVV</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise; Loss of availability</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Memory corruption or parser flaw in the communication stack of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} could be deployed with insecure defaults (services enabled, security features off, weak crypto) because secure configuration is not the default or is not documented.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'GE.P')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E12</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} could be deployed with insecure defaults (services enabled, security features off, weak crypto) because secure configuration is not the default or is not documented.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Ship secure by default. Provide a machine-readable configuration report and the ability to check settings (CR 7.6). Publish hardening and secure integration guidelines (4-1 SG).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SG - Security guidelines</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1694.001 Insecure Credentials: Default Credentials; T0866 Exploitation of Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.6; 4-2 CR 7.7; 4-1 SG</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Insecure default configuration of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Open-source or commercial components (RTOS, protocol stacks, libraries) in {target.Name} may contain known vulnerabilities or be compromised in the supply chain.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.ThirdPartyComponents is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'GE.P')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T17</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Open-source or commercial components (RTOS, protocol stacks, libraries) in {target.Name} may contain known vulnerabilities or be compromised in the supply chain.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Maintain an SBOM. Assess third-party components before use (4-1 SM-9, SM-10). Monitor vulnerability sources and handle issues through the defect management process (4-1 DM). Patch or mitigate promptly.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SM - Security management and supply chain</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0862 Supply Chain Compromise</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.8; 4-1 SM-9; 4-1 SM-10; 4-1 DM</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Vulnerable or compromised third-party component in {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} could be counterfeited or tampered with during manufacturing, shipping or provisioning, including injection of attacker-controlled keys.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T18</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} could be counterfeited or tampered with during manufacturing, shipping or provisioning, including injection of attacker-controlled keys.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Provision product-supplier roots of trust in a controlled environment (EDR/NDR 3.12) and let the asset owner provision their own (3.13). Provide device identity certificates and genuineness checks. Use tamper-evident packaging.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SM - Security management and supply chain</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0862 Supply Chain Compromise</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 EDR 3.12; 4-2 EDR 3.13; 4-1 SM</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Persistent compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Counterfeit device or tampering of {target.Name} before delivery</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker or careless user could turn off logging, authentication or filtering on {target.Name} without being noticed.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IPC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Server' or target is 'SE.P.OT.EWSHost' or target is 'SE.P.OT.PLC' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SIS' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RTU' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IED' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SmartField' or target is 'SE.P.OT.IIoT' or target is 'SE.P.OT.SafetyIO')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T19</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker or careless user could turn off logging, authentication or filtering on {target.Name} without being noticed.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Restrict security configuration to administrators. Audit configuration changes (CR 2.8). Support verification of security functions (CR 3.3) and configuration baselines (CR 7.6).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0872 Indicator Removal on Host</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.3; 4-2 CR 7.6; 4-2 CR 2.8</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Security configuration of {target.Name} disabled or weakened</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>An update to {target.Name} could fail, be interrupted or be incompatible, stopping operation with no way back.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.FieldUpdatable is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'GE.P')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An update to {target.Name} could fail, be interrupted or be incompatible, stopping operation with no way back.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Support atomic update with rollback to the last known-good image. Allow updates to be scheduled by the asset owner without affecting essential functions (EDR/HDR/NDR 3.10). Qualify patches before release (4-1 SUM).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SUM - Security update management</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0826 Loss of Availability</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.4; 4-2 EDR 3.10; 4-2 HDR 3.10; 4-2 NDR 3.10; 4-1 SUM</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of availability</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Failed or malicious update leaves {target.Name} unavailable</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>{target.Name} could use weak algorithms, short keys, poor random numbers or unmanaged certificates, making protections easy to break.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>((target is 'GE.P' and target.StoresSecrets is 'No') or flow.GenerateThreats is 'No')</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'GE.P')) and ((flow crosses 'GE.TB.L' or flow crosses 'GE.TB.B') or (source is 'GE.EI'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I08</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>{target.Name} could use weak algorithms, short keys, poor random numbers or unmanaged certificates, making protections easy to break.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use cryptography per recognised standards (CR 4.3). Support crypto agility and certificate lifecycle (CR 1.8, 1.9). Use a hardware RNG where possible.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0842 Network Sniffing; T0830 Adversary-in-the-Middle</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.3; 4-2 CR 1.8; 4-2 CR 1.9</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Weak or obsolete cryptography in {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Weak rules, any-any rules, protocol tunnelling or misconfiguration on {target.Name} could let traffic pass between zones that should be separated.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E13</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Weak rules, any-any rules, protocol tunnelling or misconfiguration on {target.Name} could let traffic pass between zones that should be separated.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Deny by default and allow only documented conduits (NDR 5.2). Use protocol-aware / DPI filtering for industrial protocols. Review rules regularly and alert on changes. Support fail-close behaviour.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0884 Connection Proxy; T0886 Remote Services; T0885 Commonly Used Port</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 NDR 5.2; 3-3 SR 5.1; 3-3 SR 5.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of segmentation</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Zone boundary bypass or misconfiguration of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker connected to {target.Name} could use VLAN hopping, ARP spoofing, rogue DHCP or unauthorised port mirroring to intercept or redirect traffic.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T20</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker connected to {target.Name} could use VLAN hopping, ARP spoofing, rogue DHCP or unauthorised port mirroring to intercept or redirect traffic.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Enable port security, DHCP snooping, dynamic ARP inspection and disable unused ports. Restrict management access. Log configuration and topology changes.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SG - Security guidelines</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0830 Adversary-in-the-Middle; T0842 Network Sniffing</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.6; 4-2 CR 7.7; 4-2 CR 3.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of control; Confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Layer 2 attacks via {target.Name} (VLAN hopping, ARP spoofing, port mirroring)</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Broadcast storms, CAM table overflow, routing / redundancy protocol attacks (MRP, RSTP) or management-plane floods could stop {target.Name} from forwarding OT traffic.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D08</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Broadcast storms, CAM table overflow, routing / redundancy protocol attacks (MRP, RSTP) or management-plane floods could stop {target.Name} from forwarding OT traffic.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Storm control and rate limiting. Protect the management plane. Authenticate redundancy and routing protocols where supported. Keep forwarding of control traffic independent of management load (CR 7.1).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SVV - Security verification and validation</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0814 Denial of Service; T0826 Loss of Availability</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.1; 4-2 CR 7.2</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of availability; Loss of view</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Denial of service of network device {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>SNMP community strings, Telnet/HTTP management or configuration backups of {target.Name} could disclose credentials and network topology.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.P.OT.Firewall' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Switch' or target is 'SE.P.OT.Router' or target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP' or target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess' or target is 'SE.P.OT.DataDiode')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I09</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SNMP community strings, Telnet/HTTP management or configuration backups of {target.Name} could disclose credentials and network topology.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use SNMPv3, SSH and HTTPS for management. Disable Telnet, HTTP and SNMPv1/v2c by default. Encrypt stored configuration backups.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SG - Security guidelines</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0842 Network Sniffing; T0888 Remote System Information Discovery</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.1; 4-2 CR 1.5; 4-2 CR 7.7</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Management credentials or configuration of {target.Name} disclosed</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>Phished or reused VPN / remote access credentials could give an attacker interactive access to {target.Name} from the Internet.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.RemoteAccess is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-S06</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Phished or reused VPN / remote access credentials could give an attacker interactive access to {target.Name} from the Internet.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Require multi-factor authentication for access from untrusted networks (CR 1.1 RE / SR 1.13). Use individual accounts. Restrict source addresses and time windows.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0822 External Remote Services; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 1.13; 4-2 CR 1.1; 4-2 CR 2.6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Stolen credentials used for remote access to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>Vendor or integrator access to {target.Name} could be always-on, unsupervised or overly broad, giving a path for attackers who compromise the third party.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((source is 'SE.EI.OT.Vendor' or source is 'SE.EI.OT.Integrator') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.RemoteAccess'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E14</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Vendor or integrator access to {target.Name} could be always-on, unsupervised or overly broad, giving a path for attackers who compromise the third party.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Enable remote access on request only, with approval and session recording. Support remote session termination (CR 2.6) and concurrent session limits (CR 2.7). Restrict third parties to the assets they support.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SG - Security guidelines</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0822 External Remote Services; T0886 Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 2.6; 3-3 SR 1.13; 4-2 CR 2.7</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR2 Use control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Unsupervised or persistent third-party access to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>E</a:Category><a:Description>The flow from {source.Name} reaches {target.Name} over the Internet, cellular or another untrusted network, so it can be found and attacked directly.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(flow crosses 'SE.TB.L.OT.Internet' or flow crosses 'SE.TB.B.OT.Cloud' or (flow.Medium is 'Cellular' or flow.Medium is 'Internet or WAN')) and (target is 'GE.P')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-E15</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The flow from {source.Name} reaches {target.Name} over the Internet, cellular or another untrusted network, so it can be found and attacked directly.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Never expose OT services directly to the Internet. Terminate untrusted connections in a DMZ / remote access gateway with MFA (SR 1.13). Monitor for exposure (e.g. Shodan-type scans of own address space).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0883 Internet Accessible Device; T0822 External Remote Services</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 5.2; 3-3 SR 1.13; 4-2 NDR 1.13</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR5 Restricted data flow</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>{target.Name} exposed to the Internet or an untrusted network</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Radio traffic to {target.Name} can be captured from outside the physical perimeter.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((flow.Medium is 'Wireless') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (source is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.WirelessIF is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I10</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Radio traffic to {target.Name} can be captured from outside the physical perimeter.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Use strong wireless security (WPA3-Enterprise, WirelessHART/ISA100 join keys managed securely). Control wireless use (CR 2.2, SR 1.6). Add application-level encryption for sensitive data.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0887 Wireless Sniffing</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 4.1; 4-2 CR 2.2; 3-3 SR 1.6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR4 Data confidentiality</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Confidentiality; Attack enablement</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Wireless sniffing of traffic to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>S</a:Category><a:Description>An attacker could set up a rogue AP or join a rogue device to the wireless network used by {target.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((flow.Medium is 'Wireless') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (source is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.WirelessIF is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-S07</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>An attacker could set up a rogue AP or join a rogue device to the wireless network used by {target.Name}.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Mutual authentication of wireless devices and networks (SR 1.6). Wireless intrusion detection. Disable unused radios (CR 7.7).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0860 Wireless Compromise; T0848 Rogue Master</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>3-3 SR 1.6; 4-2 CR 2.2; 4-2 CR 1.2; 4-2 CR 1.6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR1 Identification and authentication control</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 2</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Manipulation of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Rogue access point or rogue wireless device connecting to {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>D</a:Category><a:Description>Radio jamming or de-authentication attacks could cut wireless communication to {target.Name}.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((flow.Medium is 'Wireless') or (target is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (source is 'SE.P.OT.WirelessAP') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.WirelessIF is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-D09</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Radio jamming or de-authentication attacks could cut wireless communication to {target.Name}.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Medium</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Do not use wireless for safety-critical or time-critical control without a fail-safe on loss of communication. Use protected management frames (802.11w). Monitor link quality.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0814 Denial of Service; T0860 Wireless Compromise</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 7.1; 4-2 CR 3.6</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR7 Resource availability</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Loss of control; Loss of view</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>RF jamming or de-authentication of {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>The update server, repository or delivery path could be compromised to distribute malicious firmware or software.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.Firmware') or (source is 'SE.P.OT.UpdateService' or source is 'SE.DS.OT.Firmware'))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T21</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>The update server, repository or delivery path could be compromised to distribute malicious firmware or software.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Sign all update packages with keys protected in an HSM. Verify signature and version on the target. Protect the build and release pipeline (4-1 SM-7/SM-8). Publish hashes and security update notifications (4-1 SUM).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SUM - Security update management</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0862 Supply Chain Compromise; T1693.001 Modify Firmware: System Firmware</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.4; 4-2 EDR 3.10; 4-1 SUM; 4-1 SM</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Fleet-wide compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Compromised update channel between {source.Name} and {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>USB drives, SD cards or maintenance laptops connected to {target.Name} could carry malware (e.g. Stuxnet).</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((source is 'SE.EI.OT.RemovableMedia') or (flow.Medium is 'Removable media or file transfer') or (target is 'GE.P' and (target.RemovableMedia is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T22</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>USB drives, SD cards or maintenance laptops connected to {target.Name} could carry malware (e.g. Stuxnet).</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Disable autorun. Restrict or disable USB ports (CR 7.7). Scan media at a kiosk before use. Accept only signed files. Control portable and mobile devices (SR 2.3).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SG - Security guidelines</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0847 Replication Through Removable Media; T0864 Transient Cyber Asset; T0895 Autorun Image</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 EDR 3.2; 4-2 HDR 3.2; 4-2 CR 7.7; 3-3 SR 2.3</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Full compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Malware introduced into {target.Name} via removable media or transient device</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Logic, configuration, setpoints or recipes in {target.Name} could be modified, so the process runs with wrong or unsafe settings.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.DS.OT.ProjectFiles' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.Config' or target is 'SE.DS.OT.Recipe') or (target is 'GE.DS') and (target is 'GE.DS' and (target.ControlCritical is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T23</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Logic, configuration, setpoints or recipes in {target.Name} could be modified, so the process runs with wrong or unsafe settings.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Integrity-protect stored data (CR 3.4) with signatures or hashes checked before use. Restrict write access. Keep version history and change approvals.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T0836 Modify Parameter; T0889 Modify Program</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.4; 4-2 CR 2.1</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Safety; Product quality; Loss of control</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Tampering with control-critical data in {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>T</a:Category><a:Description>Firmware or software images stored in {target.Name} could be replaced with malicious versions before they are installed.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>(target is 'SE.DS.OT.Firmware')</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-T24</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Firmware or software images stored in {target.Name} could be replaced with malicious versions before they are installed.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Store only signed images and verify signatures at install and boot (CR 3.4, EDR 3.14). Restrict write access to the repository.</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1693.001 Modify Firmware: System Firmware; T0862 Supply Chain Compromise</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>4-2 CR 3.4; 4-2 EDR 3.14</b:string></Values><Id>IEC62443Req</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>FoundationalReq</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Foundational Requirement</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>FR3 System integrity</b:string></Values><Id>FoundationalReq</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>MinSL</Name><Label>Relevant from SL</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SL 1</b:string></Values><Id>MinSL</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>OTImpact</Name><Label>OT Consequence</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Persistent compromise</b:string></Values><Id>OTImpact</Id></ThreatMetaDatum></a:PropertiesMetaData><a:RelatedCategory i:nil="true"/><a:ShortTitle>Tampering with firmware images in {target.Name}</a:ShortTitle></a:ThreatType><a:ThreatType><a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension><a:Category>I</a:Category><a:Description>Secrets in {target.Name} could be read by an unauthorised process or user, enabling impersonation and decryption.</a:Description><a:GenerationFilters><a:Exclude>flow.GenerateThreats is 'No'</a:Exclude><a:Include>((target is 'SE.DS.OT.KeyStore') or (target is 'GE.DS') and (target is 'GE.DS' and (target.SensitiveData is 'Yes')))</a:Include></a:GenerationFilters><a:Id>OT-I11</a:Id><a:PropertiesMetaData><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name><Label>Short Description</Label><HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</b:string></Values><Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>UserThreatDescription</Name><Label>Description</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Secrets in {target.Name} could be read by an unauthorised process or user, enabling impersonation and decryption.</b:string></Values><Id>a8bfac8b-0ece-5a66-b0ff-fe6f9547b7b1</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>Priority</Name><Label>Priority</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>High</b:string></Values><Id>849869b2-a4f9-5106-8367-c47a51895cca</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>PossibleMitigations</Name><Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>Store secrets hashed (passwords) or in hardware-protected storage (keys). Restrict access to the owning process. Encrypt at rest (CR 4.1).</b:string></Values><Id>PossibleMitigations</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>SDLPhase</Name><Label>IEC 62443-4-1 Practice</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>SD - Secure by design</b:string></Values><Id>SDLPhase</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>ATTACKICS</Name><Label>MITRE ATTACK for ICS v20</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays"><b:string>T1694.002 Insecure Credentials: Hardcoded Credentials; T0859 Valid Accounts</b:string></Values><Id>ATTACKICS</Id></ThreatMetaDatum><ThreatMetaDatum><Name>IEC62443Req</Name><Label>IEC 62443 Requirement(s)</Label><HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI><Values xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/20